  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "藝術的眼睛：從古典到近代的美感探索",
    "sub_ename": "THE EYE OF ART: EXPLORING AESTHETIC IDEAS FROM CLASSICAL TO EARLY MODERN TIMES",
    "describe_ch": "本課程探討藝術與美學觀念的歷史演變，聚焦西方自古典至近代的美學思想，並比較東亞（中國、日本）藝術傳統。學生將學習觀察藝術形式、理解文化意涵，思考藝術如何反映與形塑價值觀。內容涵蓋古典藝術、中古世紀、文藝復興、啟蒙時代、浪漫主義與工業時代的藝術發展，並以講授、討論、發表進行，強調主動學習與跨文化視野。課程含小型創作活動與期末專題，結合理論與實作，培養分析、表達與創意能力。",
    "describe_eh": "This course explores the evolution of artistic and aesthetic concepts from ancient Greece to the pre-modern era, alongside Chinese and Japanese traditions for cross-cultural comparison. Students examine how art reflects and shapes cultural values through shifting ideas of beauty and ugliness. The course covers the development of artistic expression from ancient Greece through the Middle Ages, Renaissance, Enlightenment, Romanticism, and the Industrial Age. Teaching methods include lectures, discussions, and presentations to promote active learning and critical thinking. Each unit features a creative assignment that encourages hands-on exploration of artistic styles within cultural contexts. The semester concludes with a final project integrating visual analysis, cultural reflection, and artistic creation.",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 2.0
  },
